  "mathematicalDefectDiagnosis" : "Mathematical Root Cause Verified: In BalancedDetectionLoss, the negative confidence loss is normalized by dividing by normNeg (the number of background cells, ~8,170 per batch), whereas the positive confidence loss is normalized by normPos (~16 per batch). When multiplied by bgWeight=0.5, the gradient for each negative cell is scaled by 0.5 / normNeg = 0.000061, compared to 1.0 / normPos = 0.0625 for a positive cell (a 1,022:1 asymmetry). Solving the zero-gradient equilibrium equation (sigmoid(p) - 1) + 0.5 * sigmoid(p) = 0 yields an expected prediction probability of exactly 1 / (1 + 0.5) = 0.667 (66.7%). Consequently, untrained/uncertain background cells converge to ~66.7% confidence, floating above the arbitrary 0.55 threshold and generating ~41.5% cell activation across background frames."
